course: dictionary
lesson: 9949
title: Task: a job to do
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A task is a piece of work that someone has to do, often one given to you by someone else. «Your task is to write three sentences» tells you exactly what to do, and when the sentences are written, the task is finished.
explain: Task can also be a verb, but it is formal. To be tasked with something means you have been given a job to do. «Take someone to task» is a set phrase that means to tell someone off for something they did, so the context tells you which meaning is used.
explain: Big tasks are easier when you break them into small steps. In a timed task, «the plan must be short: a few minutes and a few words per part», and a few minutes at the end are saved for checking. Always ask: what is the task, and what does it want me to do?
fact: A task is a piece of work that someone has to do.
fact: «Starting a task before all the instructions are given often leads to mistakes.»
fact: «On task» means concentrating on your work, and «off task» means not working.
fact: «Take someone to task» means to tell them off for something they did.
fact: Tasked is a formal verb: to be tasked with something means you have been given a job to do.
exercise: «Your task is to write three sentences.» What is a task here? | A game you play at break | A place to sit in class | A kind of pencil | *A piece of work you have to do
exercise: «Starting a task before all the instructions are given often leads to mistakes.» What does this sentence advise you to do? | *Wait until all the instructions are given | Ask for a new task | Start straight away, before anything else | Skip the instructions
exercise: Mrs Patel says, «Ravi, you are off task.» What does off task mean? | Sitting at the front of the room | Working very quickly | Finished and ready to go home | *Not working or not concentrating
test: The teacher says, «I am tasking you with tidying the library.» What does tasking mean here? | *Giving you a job to do | Lending you a book | Asking you to stop reading | Telling you off for being late
test: «Her mum took her to task for leaving her bike in the rain.» What does took to task mean? | Took her out for a treat | Helped her clean the bike | *Told her off for it | Gave her a new bike
exam: «In a timed task, a few minutes at the end are saved for checking.» What is the best way to use those last few minutes? | Start a brand new task | Read a comic | Pack your bag and leave | *Check your work
